---
// About Abimbola. The story is her own text (Light_Cakes_About_Me.docx,
// Nov 2026), only regrouped into paragraphs. Keep it in her words: this page is
// where the "real person who bakes by hand" comes through.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import Photo from "../components/Photo.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
import { photos } from "../photos";
import { whatsappLink } from "../site";

// A few bakes to show alongside her story
const bakes = [photos.childrens.fairyGarden, photos.wedding.whiteRufflesGreenery, photos.birthday.navyGoldMyKing];
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About · LightCakes"
	description="Meet Abimbola, the baker behind LightCakes — bespoke cakes and branded treats, baked by hand in Leeds."
>
	<PageHeader
		eyebrow="The person behind it"
		title="Hello, I'm Abimbola"
		intro="I'm the baker behind LightCakes. Every cake and treat is designed and baked by hand in my kitchen in Leeds."
	>
		<!-- object-top: when the box crops the photo, keep her face, lose the bottom -->
		<Photo slot="aside" {...photos.about.abimbolaPortrait} eager class="h-96 object-top lg:h-140" />
	</PageHeader>

	<Prose>
		<h2>The heart behind LightCakes</h2>
		<p>
			LightCakes started in my heart when I was just a young girl growing up in my home country, Nigeria. I was in JSS 1
			at the time, and I had the opportunity to be selected as one of the representatives to represent my school at a
			special Children's Day programme.
		</p>
		<p>
			We participated in all the activities, and eventually, it was time for the cake-cutting ceremony. Coming from a
			humble home, I had never tasted cake before, let alone a good-quality cake. So, when we were given a piece of cake,
			I took my first bite, and honestly, I could not explain what I was tasting. It was so good! I couldn't quite place
			the taste. I kept wondering, “What is this? What could this be? How was this made?”
		</p>
		<p>
			I was genuinely fascinated and curious. I wanted to understand what went into making something that tasted so
			incredibly good. And just like that, a fire was ignited in me that day. I remember thinking, “I want to make this
			sort of cake too!” That little experience planted a seed in my heart, a seed that would eventually grow into
			LightCakes.
		</p>
		<p>
			I understand that we are now in a generation where cakes are much more accessible, and almost everyone has had the
			opportunity to taste different types of cakes at some point. It is not quite like it used to be back then. However,
			my dream remains the same: I want to ensure that whoever tastes my cake will have an experience that leaves a
			lasting impression.
		</p>
		<p>
			Beyond the taste, I want my cakes to inspire. I want to inspire a child who might discover a passion for baking
			after tasting one of my cakes. I want to inspire a young person to develop an interest, explore a dream and believe
			in what is possible. I even want to inspire someone older to pick up a dream they may have thought was too late to
			pursue.
		</p>
		<p>
			And for those who may not have any interest in baking at all, I simply want to create exceptional experiences for
			them. I want my cakes to make their celebrations and special occasions truly memorable. And that, in essence, is
			how LightCakes was birthed.
		</p>

		<h2>More than baking — a heart for giving</h2>
		<p>
			There is another important part of my story that I want you to know. Coming from a humble background has shaped the
			way I see life and the importance of giving. I understand that there are people who need a helping hand, a little
			support and sometimes just an opportunity to experience a better tomorrow.
		</p>
		<p>
			This is why giving back is an integral part of the LightCakes journey. For every order placed, a particular
			percentage goes towards the LightCakes Foundation, which is dedicated to supporting children and individuals in
			need, particularly back home in Nigeria.
		</p>
		<p>
			So, when you place an order with us, you are not just getting value for your money or purchasing a cake for a
			special occasion. You are also contributing to something meaningful. You are helping us extend love, kindness and
			support to those who need it.
		</p>
		<p>
			It is my hope that through LightCakes, we can continue to touch lives, make a difference and put smiles on faces,
			even in our own little way.
		</p>

		<!-- Her closing line, set apart as a quote. Rose is fine here: 24px+ text only
		     needs 3:1 contrast. -->
		<blockquote class="my-10 border-l-2 border-pink pl-6 font-display text-2xl leading-tight text-rose italic">
			Because to me, LightCakes is more than just baking cakes. It is about creating beautiful memories, inspiring lives
			and spreading light, one cake at a time.
		</blockquote>
		<p>Thank you for being part of my story and the LightCakes journey.</p>
		<p class="font-display text-xl">— Abimbola</p>
	</Prose>

	<!-- A FEW RECENT BAKES -->
	<section class="bg-sand">
		<div class="mx-auto flex max-w-content flex-col gap-6 px-5 py-14 lg:px-14">
			<h2 class="text-center text-2xl">A few recent bakes</h2>
			<ul class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-3">
				{
					bakes.map((photo) => (
						<li>
							<Photo {...photo} sizes="(min-width: 640px) 33vw, 100vw" class="h-80 lg:h-96" />
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ul>
			<a
				href="/gallery"
				class="flex min-h-11 items-center self-center text-sm font-semibold text-ink underline underline-offset-4"
			>
				See the full gallery <span aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;→</span>
			</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<CtaBand title="Let's make something together" text="Tell me about your occasion — I'd love to hear what you have in mind.">
		<Button href="/enquire">Start an enquiry</Button>
		<Button href={whatsappLink("Hi Abimbola, I'd like to ask about an order.")} variant="outline">
			Message on WhatsApp
		</Button>
	</CtaBand>
</BaseLayout>
